# Deny-all with an explicit allowlist.
#
# ~/.claude is BOTH this repo's checkout and Claude Code's live runtime
# directory: session transcripts, prompt history, plans, caches and per-project
# auto-memory all accrete here. An ignore list that enumerates runtime dirs goes
# stale the moment the CLI adds a new one, and the failure mode is publishing
# session content to a PUBLIC repo. So: ignore everything, then re-admit the
# handful of directories that are actually shared config.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/agents/
!/commands/
!/rules/
!/skills/
!/hooks/
!/README.md
!/LICENSE

# settings.json is deliberately NOT tracked. It carries machine-local
# configuration — internal hostnames, private subdomains, object-store buckets
# and database schema names — and this repo is public. Keep user settings
# machine-local; the repo is a portable toolkit, not a settings store.

# Never share, even from an allowlisted directory.
*.log
*.bak
*.bak.*
.DS_Store
.skill-execution-context.json
